# The pulseengine/zephyr revision every gale CI job builds against.
#
# CI used to clone the BRANCH (`west init --mr gale/sem-replacement`), so a run's
# Zephyr was whatever that branch held at the time, and no gale commit recorded it —
# a result was not reproducible from gale's history alone. gale#401's 38 -> 0 kernel
# delta spanned exactly such a branch change (pulseengine/zephyr#1).
#
# Bumping this file is how gale takes a fork change, reviewably, like any other pin.
# A gate (.github/workflows/compliance.yml) fails if this revision is no longer an
# ancestor of gale/sem-replacement — i.e. the fork was rebased or force-pushed away
# from it — because then this pin names a commit the fork no longer contains.
